```c
void printMatrix(int rows, int cols, int matrix[rows][cols]) {
    // Or: void printMatrix(int rows, int cols, int matrix[][cols])
    // Or: void printMatrix(int rows, int cols, int (*matrix)[cols])
    // ... function body ...
}
```
The column dimension (`cols`) is mandatory because the compiler needs it to correctly calculate the memory address of elements in subsequent rows. For `matrix[i][j]`, the compiler calculates the offset for the `i`-th row as `i * cols * sizeof(int)`. Without `cols`, it cannot perform this pointer arithmetic to find the start of each row.

